udy include that they used a  strain of rats known to have really high  rates of tumors making it the exact  wrong type of rat that you would  to use for the test they had a very  small sample size and a number of  conflicts of interest were uncovered in  terms of the participants the immediate  and sort of more ancillary participants  to that study so that study is out and  there have been many studies which find  no dangers from GMOs which gets me to  the next typical anti GMO talking point  which is hey David listen it's possible  that GMOs aren't damaging to human  health but we just don't know if GMOs  are unhealthy for humans because we  don't have any long-term testing and  GMOs are so new and of course that's  wrong GMOs have been studied extensively  they first appeared in labs 30 years ago  they've been sold commercially since  1994 there are 1700 peer-reviewed safety  studies about GMOs period now to be  clear I have no horse in this I know  people will say either because of Soros  or because I'm Jewish or because I'm a  shill or because I'm in the pocket of  the big food industry or whatever listen  I have no horse in this you can be damn  sure that if I thought science supported  GMOs being unhealthy I would be leading  the charge against GMOs however that's  not where the evidence is pointing 141  Nobel laureates support GMO food and  have signed on to a document making that  clear the attempt to discredit those 141  Nobel laureates is literally out of the  climate denier handbook the skeptics or  the anti GMO people are saying okay fine  listen these are Nobel laureates but  their work isn't directly related to  GMOs so what the hell do they know which  is the same thing we hear from the write  about climate science they say a lot of  those so-called scientists don't  actually work in climatology even if  they work in related fields but when you  look at the list of the hundred and  forty-one Nobel laureates who say were  in favor of GMO food they work in  chemistry they work in medicine which  are very related to GMOs others  admittedly work in physics and economics  those are less  related to GMOs but the point is the  consensus from people working in a  variety of fields on this is that there  is not evidence that GMOs are harmful to  human health on the basis of being  genetically modified sadly lots of the  same people who fall for the anti GMO  stuff are the same people who fall for  things labeled all-natural  or derived from natural ingredients on  food products and unfortunately there's  also crossover between the anti-vaxxers  and the anti GMO people so you know I  think my main point here Pat is to just  point out that number one the idea that  I would have any interest in hiding that  GMOs are bad for people if that's what I  believe is crazy I mean there's no  sensible way that someone could make  that argument this program is not the  type of thing big pharma big agriculture  would even be interested in funding and  that's absolutely and totally silly but  most importantly there are people who on  most issues follow the science and then  on one issue sometimes it's vaccinations  sometimes it's GMO sometimes it's Russia  gate whatever they seem to be  disconnected from the facts on one  particular issue like it's their blind  spot in a sense right it's poor critical  thinking and I'm not a scientist so my  approach to it is to just trust the  overwhelming scientific majority's  opinion and that's what I do when it  comes to climate change and that's what  I do with GMOs I guess you know another  concern is labeling foods that are using  GMOs and I think that's something I can  get behind just from a consumers rights  perspective I think if people don't want  to consume GMOs they should be allowed  to make that choice and they should know  what they're putting into their bodies  well that's sort of a separate issue  it's a separate issue and I agree with  you that I'm totally fine with that  labeling I think in 15 years that labor  labeling will be silly and redundant  because basically everything will be  genetically modified to some degree so  I'm totally fine with that I have zero  opposition to that I think it's fine I  think in 15 years it's going to be seen  as a completely irrelevant thing and  sort of along those lines  there are other issues with GMOs that  are ancillary issues like for example  patented seeds which can be modified to  not produce more seeds or to concentrate  the ability to grow food by large  corporations those are things related to  GMO which are problems but they don't go  to the health of the GMOs so let's  criticize that using pesticides  alongside GMO food I don't like that  that's a problem we've got to critically  analyze each pesticide to see if it's  harmful to human health but that's  separate than the health of the food on  the basis of being genetically modified  there's another issue when we look at  crops which might be genetically  modified or not that are damaging to the  environment look at soybeans for example  soybeans require lime and synthetic  fertilizer to grow in large quantities  growing soybeans damages soil in ways  that other crops don't don't it can hurt  biodiversity it can contribute the soul  soil erosion those are issues with  soybeans whether or not they've been  genetically modified and totally  separate from the human health effects  of that genetic modification anyway  these are some examples but GMO by  virtue merely of being GMO shouldn't be  targeted by activists until we have  actual evidence that it's bad for us and  right now we simply don't have good  evidence that that's the case we have a  great program for you today I will be  taking calls I will be answering  questions we are going to so Monday I am  scheduled to have jury duty and I'm  going to find out later today whether I  have to report or not I'm hoping that I  don't and that I can be here hosting the  show on Monday if not we have gotten a  tentative agreement from Ferran cousins  of Ring of Fire he is going to be  standing by for the call from the court  if I have to be in court on Monday  Ferran cousins will be here on Monday  guest hosting the show but in any case  then the rest of the week unless I get  pulled into  big trial I will be here great program  today great bonus show thanks for being  with us one of today's sponsors is  Skillshare which is an amazing online  learning community that offers thousands  of high quality classes on almost any  topic first 500 people who click the  link under this video will get two  entire months of totally free access to  every single class offered by Skillshare  they've got classes on everything from  design video editing photography  business technology cooking meditation  even classes on personal productivity I  know you'll be able to find something on  Skillshare that fascinates you or even  something that will help you in your  everyday life classes are taught by real  people who care about what they're  teaching I just took a really great  class on more advanced video editing  techniques the david pakman show is  giving you two months of free access to  every class they offer when you click  the link under this video  think about everything you'll have at  your fingertips for two whole months  totally free hard to beat and after that  if you like it you can keep access to  every class on Skillshare for under ten  bucks a month one of the most affordable  learning platforms out there just click  the link under this video to redeem your  to three months of skill share but hurry  it's only available to the first 500 who  sign up

